  <NugetDependency Id="xg3loqNa8qGji3wC7xSOJO" Location="VL.CoreLib" />
  <DocumentDependency Id="0d9wDN3bn0FISx6baVtyXH" Location="../../VL.Qt.vl" />
  <Patch Id="ioUlsdV5hAGcaf361CACJV">
    <Canvas Id="29oTCdUsHtGboxKrrkyFSN" DefaultCategory="Main" BordersChecked="false" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,180" Id="FUvPKtZp3FGiDcOHN8O27F">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="qclofIxCZyF2XaG6WdLSDN">
        <Canvas Id="q7QqUWrcmvFQ9MFz6L0aUM" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="26u395zcO1FIAu0WxbBuQB" Bounds="85,16,710,52" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="How To Create Shader Nodes from Files">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">25</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="vLz5eWhpCyGAP5bya08eOL" Bounds="85,85,520,94" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Shader nodes from qtshaders/*.frag&#xD;&#xA;- Folder qtshaders next to this patch: one node per .frag, one pin per uniform&#xD;&#xA;- sampler2D source = Input pin (filter, 1), without it a generator (2)&#xD;&#xA;- Annotations: @default, @min, @max, @color, @summary&#xD;&#xA;- Category Qt.Elements.Shaders, or @category in the file head">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="AUNpDXtMTQG7seDJlWy2SC" Bounds="85,819,830,427" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Subfolders of qtshaders count, too. The node is named like the file: RGBSplit.frag gives the node RGBSplit. A .vert with the same name belongs to it.&#xD;&#xA;- @summary in the file head is the help text of the node. An extra sampler2D becomes an image pin.&#xD;&#xA;- Every other uniform in the uniform block becomes a pin, the camel case name split into words (colorA gives Color A), in the order of the file. Supported: float, vec2, vec3, vec4, int, bool, mat4.&#xD;&#xA;- Annotations are // comments above the uniform or at the end of its line: @min and @max are limits of the pad only (nothing is clamped), @color turns a vec4 into a color (components 0..1), @summary is the help text of the pin.&#xD;&#xA;- Blending, Size, Transform and the hidden pins work like on ShaderEffect.&#xD;&#xA;- The nodes appear when the qtshaders folder exists next to the saved patch. New, renamed or deleted files update the node browser while vvvv runs.&#xD;&#xA;- Save the .frag and the node updates. Pins with the same name keep their links and values. A shader with a compile error shows the error with its line number at the node; the pins of the last valid state stay.&#xD;&#xA;- Unknown annotations and unsupported uniform types (uint, ivec, mat3, arrays) show as warnings at the node, the pin is skipped or takes its default.&#xD;&#xA;- The shader is full Qt GLSL 440, like in the ShaderEffect node (see HowTo Write a ShaderEffect): the uniform block starts with qt_Matrix and qt_Opacity, the output is premultiplied. qtshaders/RGBSplit.frag and Stripes.frag are commented as templates, open them in an editor next to this patch.&#xD;&#xA;- Two .frag files with the same name in one qtshaders tree give an error at both nodes. A .vert without a .frag makes no node.&#xD;&#xA;- A filter (with sampler2D source) also appears as a node in Qt.Effects, same name, with Output and Error: it chains like Blur or DropShadow on the Effect pin of an element. @padding in the file head (DIP) lets it draw beyond the element. See HowTo Chain Shader Effects.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="ljKxMTIHhjGvhBKa6lMbWK" Bounds="88,272,480,65" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="1  RGBSplit.frag is a filter: its sampler2D source is the Input pin. Amount (DIP) has @min/@max, Direction a @default, Tint is a @color, Scanlines a bool.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="t17z7NAocpFCcbVKoUDImD" Bounds="605,272,480,65" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="2  Stripes.frag is a generator: no Input pin. The Size pin sets its size, an LFO drives Phase, Count and the two colors keep their @default.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
